.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH QUIPU 1 "" quipu "Quipu Manual"
.SH NAME
quipu \- AI\-native knowledge graph with strict ontology enforcement
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquipu\fR [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quipu stores RDF facts in one SQLite file, queries them with SPARQL, validates writes against SHACL shapes and keeps every fact\*(Aqs transaction and valid time. `qp` is the same binary under its short name. Run `quipu prime` for an agent primer.
.PP
Store commands operate on a local database (\-\-db, default .bobbin/quipu/quipu.db; configuration may override it), not the HTTP service. Help never reads configuration or opens a store.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Store file (default: .bobbin/quipu/quipu.db; configuration may override it)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
quipu\-store(1)
Inspect native ownership, or explicitly adopt or restore a disk store
.TP
quipu\-version(1)
Print the version and source commit
.TP
quipu\-install\-alias(1)
Add the qp alias beside the quipu binary
.TP
quipu\-knot(1)
Assert Turtle facts, validated against loaded shapes
.TP
quipu\-load(1)
Assert Turtle facts (alias of knot), or load a project bundle directory
.TP
quipu\-ingest(1)
Bulk\-load an N\-Triples, Turtle or N\-Quads file into one graph with declared count and digest
.TP
quipu\-read(1)
Run a SPARQL query, optionally as of a valid time or transaction
.TP
quipu\-query(1)
Run a SPARQL query (alias of read)
.TP
quipu\-rule\-query(1)
Read typed ROOT support and the admitted judgment for a rule request
.TP
quipu\-cord(1)
List entities, optionally of one type
.TP
quipu\-unravel(1)
Show facts as they were at a transaction or valid time
.TP
quipu\-impact(1)
Walk what depends on an entity, optionally after a speculative removal
.TP
quipu\-explain(1)
Trace a derived fact back to its premises
.TP
quipu\-project(1)
Project the graph and run a graph algorithm such as PageRank
.TP
quipu\-report(1)
Report hubs, surprising links and open questions in the graph
.TP
quipu\-reason(1)
Run Datalog rules to a fixpoint and persist the derivations
.TP
quipu\-demotions(1)
Read preserved unsupported demotions without materializing a closure
.TP
quipu\-episode(1)
Ingest a structured episode of nodes and edges from JSON
.TP
quipu\-retract(1)
Retract an entity\*(Aqs facts, optionally one predicate; history is kept
.TP
quipu\-shapes(1)
Load, list or remove the SHACL shapes that guard writes
.TP
quipu\-namespaces(1)
List or apply the owner namespace registry
.TP
quipu\-entity\-ref(1)
Mint or resolve stable entity references
.TP
quipu\-ontology(1)
Load, list or remove OWL ontologies (owl feature)
.TP
quipu\-validate(1)
Validate a data file against a shapes file without writing
.TP
quipu\-repl(1)
Open an interactive SPARQL prompt
.TP
quipu\-export(1)
Export RDF from ROOT, one graph, a provenance group or a CONSTRUCT query
.TP
quipu\-render(1)
Render graph data into files in an owned directory
.TP
quipu\-stats(1)
Show store statistics
.TP
quipu\-prime(1)
Print the agent primer and a bounded, read\-only summary of the store
.TP
quipu\-search(1)
Search entities by keyword, vector or hybrid ranking
.TP
quipu\-search\-index(1)
Report, backfill or drop the search indexes
.TP
quipu\-doctor(1)
Report graph\-label drift and recommended floors
.TP
quipu\-pack(1)
Export a graph, or the whole store, as a pack; or verify a pack
.TP
quipu\-unpack(1)
Merge a published pack into a local graph
.TP
quipu\-restore(1)
Replace the store with a full pack, binary or text
.TP
quipu\-share(1)
Write a portable share of a graph, scope or project
.TP
quipu\-status(1)
Report how a share has diverged from this store
.TP
quipu\-merge(1)
Merge a share back into ROOT, with reviewable conflict decisions
.TP
quipu\-import(1)
Verify a share into quarantine, then promote or review it
.TP
quipu\-compose(1)
Compose verified packs into a named inspection dataset
.TP
quipu\-changes(1)
Read whole transaction change pages from the change feed
.TP
quipu\-follow(1)
Keep this database a read\-only follower of a primary server
.TP
quipu\-acquire(1)
Measure the bounded scope of a direct\-main graph acquisition
.TP
quipu\-migrate\-vectors(1)
Move stored vectors between backends (lancedb feature)
.TP
quipu\-git\-merge(1)
Merge pendants from Git snapshots and stop before committing
.TP
quipu\-merge\-driver(1)
Low\-level Git merge driver for pendant files
.TP
quipu\-pendant\-resolve(1)
Record a resolution choice for one pendant merge conflict
.TP
quipu\-pendant\-check(1)
Check a pendant merge result in CI without a merge driver
.TP
quipu\-diff\-textconv(1)
Render a pack with labels for git diff textconv
.TP
quipu\-mcp(1)
Serve the MCP tools over stdio through the sibling quipu\-server
.TP
quipu\-hook(1)
Run a harness hook such as session capture
.TP
quipu\-hooks(1)
Bundle, install, uninstall or check quipu\*(Aqs Claude Code and Codex hooks
.TP
quipu\-policy(1)
Draft an advisory policy from an exemplar, or backtest one
.TP
quipu\-gate(1)
Judge a candidate policy set over recorded history without writing
.TP
quipu\-path(1)
Golden\-path analysis: provenance cone, backtest and draft
.TP
quipu\-align(1)
Propose, decide and apply cross\-graph alignments
.TP
quipu\-propose(1)
List, submit, plan, accept or reject schema change proposals
.TP
quipu\-memory(1)
Read, export, receipt or commit versioned file memory
.TP
quipu\-attest(1)
Register and manage attested session bindings
.TP
quipu\-signer(1)
Enroll and manage hardware signers for attested writes
.TP
quipu\-deck(1)
Configure and enroll the Decision Deck
.TP
quipu\-trust\-root(1)
Enroll the first human key of the root of trust
.TP
quipu\-graph(1)
Create, label, list, import, freeze and thaw named graphs and overlays
.TP
quipu\-db(1)
Respace, attach or migrate the store file
.TP
quipu\-events(1)
Read store event records such as refusals
.TP
quipu\-fork(1)
Create, list, diff, drop or promote named forks of ROOT
.TP
quipu\-audit(1)
Check traces, namespaces, replays and quarantine against policy
